{
 "id": "puc2-maths-02-inverse-trigonometric-functions.t1.lesson",
 "chapterId": "puc2-maths-02-inverse-trigonometric-functions",
 "topicId": "puc2-maths-02-inverse-trigonometric-functions.t1",
 "title": {
  "en": "Inverse sine and inverse cosine",
  "kn": "ವಿಲೋಮ ಸೈನ್ ಮತ್ತು ವಿಲೋಮ ಕೊಸೈನ್"
 },
 "minutes": 40,
 "blocks": [
  {
   "id": "intro",
   "type": "intro",
   "heading": {
    "en": "Which angle has sine 1/2?",
    "kn": "ಯಾವ ಕೋನದ ಸೈನ್ 1/2?"
   },
   "hook": {
    "en": "sin 30°, sin 150° and sin 390° are all 1/2. If we ask \"which angle has sine one half?\", we must agree on one answer. That agreement is the principal value.",
    "kn": "sin 30°, sin 150°, sin 390° ಎಲ್ಲವೂ 1/2. \"ಯಾವ ಕೋನದ ಸೈನ್ 1/2?\" ಎಂದು ಕೇಳಿದರೆ ಒಂದೇ ಉತ್ತರ ಬೇಕು. ಆ ಒಪ್ಪಿತ ಉತ್ತರವೇ ಮುಖ್ಯ ಬೆಲೆ."
   },
   "objectives": [
    {
     "en": "Restrict sine and cosine to make them one-one"
    },
    {
     "en": "State the domain and range of sin⁻¹ and cos⁻¹"
    },
    {
     "en": "Find principal values"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "sin 30°, sin 150° and sin 390° are all 1/2. If we ask \"which angle has sine one half?\", we must agree on one answer. That agreement is the principal value.",
    "kn": "sin 30°, sin 150°, sin 390° ಎಲ್ಲವೂ 1/2. \"ಯಾವ ಕೋನದ ಸೈನ್ 1/2?\" ಎಂದು ಕೇಳಿದರೆ ಒಂದೇ ಉತ್ತರ ಬೇಕು. ಆ ಒಪ್ಪಿತ ಉತ್ತರವೇ ಮುಖ್ಯ ಬೆಲೆ."
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "concept1",
   "type": "concept",
   "title": {
    "en": "Why restrict the domain?"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "sin is not one-one on $R$: $\\sin 0 = \\sin \\pi = 0$. On $[-\\pi/2, \\pi/2]$ it is one-one and takes every value in $[-1, 1]$, so it has an inverse there: $\\sin^{-1} : [-1, 1] \\to [-\\pi/2, \\pi/2]$. This interval is the principal value branch.",
    "kn": "R ಮೇಲೆ sin ಏಕೈಕವಲ್ಲ. [−π/2, π/2] ನಲ್ಲಿ ಅದು ಏಕೈಕ ಮತ್ತು [−1, 1] ನ ಎಲ್ಲ ಬೆಲೆಗಳನ್ನು ಪಡೆಯುತ್ತದೆ. ಆದ್ದರಿಂದ sin⁻¹ : [−1, 1] → [−π/2, π/2]. ಇದೇ ಮುಖ್ಯ ಬೆಲೆಯ ಶಾಖೆ."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "sin⁻¹ x is an angle, not 1/sin x"
    },
    {
     "en": "Domain of sin⁻¹: [−1, 1]"
    },
    {
     "en": "Range (principal branch): [−π/2, π/2]"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "Sine is not one-one on all real numbers, so we keep only the piece from minus pi by 2 to pi by 2. There it has an inverse, sin inverse, with domain minus one to one.",
    "kn": "R ಮೇಲೆ sin ಏಕೈಕವಲ್ಲ. [−π/2, π/2] ನಲ್ಲಿ ಅದು ಏಕೈಕ ಮತ್ತು [−1, 1] ನ ಎಲ್ಲ ಬೆಲೆಗಳನ್ನು ಪಡೆಯುತ್ತದೆ. ಆದ್ದರಿಂದ sin⁻¹ : [−1, 1] → [−π/2, π/2]. ಇದೇ ಮುಖ್ಯ ಬೆಲೆಯ ಶಾಖೆ."
   },
   "formula": "\\sin^{-1} : [-1, 1] \\to \\left[-\\tfrac{\\pi}{2}, \\tfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right]"
  },
