   "title": {
    "en": "Inverse cosine"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "cos is one-one on $[0, \\pi]$ and takes every value in $[-1, 1]$ there. So $\\cos^{-1} : [-1, 1] \\to [0, \\pi]$. For a negative input the angle lies in $(\\pi/2, \\pi]$.",
    "kn": "cos, [0, π] ನಲ್ಲಿ ಏಕೈಕ. ಆದ್ದರಿಂದ cos⁻¹ : [−1, 1] → [0, π]. ಋಣ ಬೆಲೆಗೆ ಕೋನ (π/2, π] ನಲ್ಲಿ ಇರುತ್ತದೆ."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "Domain of cos⁻¹: [−1, 1]"
    },
    {
     "en": "Range: [0, π]"
    },
    {
     "en": "cos⁻¹(−x) = π − cos⁻¹ x"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "For cosine we keep the piece from zero to pi. So cos inverse takes values from minus one to one and gives angles from zero to pi.",
    "kn": "cos, [0, π] ನಲ್ಲಿ ಏಕೈಕ. ಆದ್ದರಿಂದ cos⁻¹ : [−1, 1] → [0, π]. ಋಣ ಬೆಲೆಗೆ ಕೋನ (π/2, π] ನಲ್ಲಿ ಇರುತ್ತದೆ."
   },
   "formula": "\\cos^{-1} : [-1, 1] \\to [0, \\pi]"
  },
